  "details": "VRChat Version: VRChat 2021.1.1p1\nDescription of the bug: When looking in the distance on multiple larger scale maps, the objects are culled only when in my direct line of sight. However, they will show up when I look at them with my peripheral vision, almost 90 degrees either direction away from it. Basically, the edges are rendering the meshes but the center is not, the exact opposite expected results to occlusion culling. I am using WindowsMR on the Odyssey+, and others on different headsets (namely the quest 2 w/ a link cable on steamvr) report that they can see the same objects without issue. The culling works as expected in non-vr mode.\nSteps to reproduce (how did you encounter the bug?): Anytime I choose a larger map and move my head side to side, the mesh only renders at the edges and disappears in the center. Yet, others see the mesh entirely.\nAny extra files? (output logs, screenshots): GIF attached of turning head, meshes unloading and loading clearly seen at the edges.",
